WEBVTT

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:04.240
Finally Arrived

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:08.210
Wake up! Wake up!

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:09.890
Wake up, everyone!

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.320
What is it, so early?

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.680
Look! Take a look out front!

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:22.230
Look, everyone. Take a good look.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:23.730
It's the mainland!

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:34.340
We've finally... arrived.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:42.370
At the end of our harsh voyage, we'd finally managed to reach the mainland.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:48.780
What an amazin' place!

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:53.430
Anyways, we all safely crossed the ocean.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:54.410
That's true.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:56.920
Now it's crossing land!

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.430
I'm sure we can do it.

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:02.510
And once we go, we won't fall into the sea either.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:07.120
Yeah! We won't have to worry about almost bein' eaten by a fish, like a certain someone.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.580
Shut up!

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.720
Chako, look for a place we might be able to land.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:14.690
Okay!

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:20.960
We're..

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.240
...somewhere 'round here.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:27.030
About ten kilometres north of here there's an estuary.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:30.480
For now we should turn into the river 'n continue from there.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:31.640
Let's do it.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:48.860
Wow.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:50.960
This is the first time I've seen something like this.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:52.830
They had them in amusement parks.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:54.670
Those were manmade.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.090
I know.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:00.480
There wasn't any real nature in our colony.

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:08.660
Howard's stomach clock's right on time.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:11.390
Everyone's hungry, right?

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.390
Yep, I'm hungry.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:16.680
Me too. It's about time to get lunch ready.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:18.180
Yes, that's true.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:26.360
Hey! Let's have lunch somewhere that's not shaking for once.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:44.320
Getting off!

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:45.480
Alright!

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:48.410
It's the ground, the ground!

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:50.410
It's terra firma!

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:53.360
At least help a little!

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:54.860
That's dangerous!

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:57.070
Because you're always goofing off!

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.390
Sharla, give me a hand.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:00.740
Okay.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.560
I kinda wanna eat something different.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:19.940
Don't ask for luxury.

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:21.070
That's right.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:23.510
Whatever it is, we have to eat it.

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:25.420
A toast to the chef!

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.080
Sharla, you've become stronger.

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:41.430
Sure have.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:45.370
You're certainly a different person from when we were in school.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:46.830
Do you think?

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.190
I think so too myself.

00:05:55.570 --> 00:06:00.330
If my Mom and Dad would be pretty surprised if they saw me now.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:05.690
After all, they both thought of me as a child, no matter how old I got.

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:07.680
Everyone's family is like that.

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:14.170
Whenever I went to school, my Mom would ask, "Do you have this? Do you have that?"

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:18.410
No helping that. You really are a child, after all.

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:20.730
I especially don't want to hear that from you!

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:22.120
What?

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:23.990
What do you mean by that?

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:24.890
Nothing.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:26.580
What's with that way of talking?

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:27.740
Like I said, nothing.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:30.140
You should try acting more childish.

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:30.970
Why?

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:34.040
Then you'd be loved by all, just like me!

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:36.260
Howard, were you self-conscious at all?

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:37.010
Yep!

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:50.990
Mom and Dad...

00:06:58.010 --> 00:06:59.840
The main computer is here.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:03.860
There may be a space ship we can use to go back to the colony.

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:08.730
There might be clues about Adam's Mom or Dad there too!

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:11.470
Pretty far...

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:16.790
There's small terraformin' machines for changin' the climate set up here 'n there.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.010
Kinda like branch offices, I guess.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.870
Do you mind if I fish in the river for a while?

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:24.630
Go ahead.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:28.680
Let's rest here all day.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.940
It feel kinda like I'm still shaking.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:34.380
I'm still shaking too.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:38.020
'Cuz we were all swayin' for so long. It's only natural.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:39.410
That's true.

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:43.380
Now I really feel like I'm shaking again.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:44.280
It's true.

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:45.970
We really <i>are</i> shaking!

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:52.830
--What's this?
--What?

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:53.810
An earthquake!

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:54.970
An earthquake!?

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:58.120
What's an earthquake?

00:07:59.130 --> 00:07:59.960
Sharla!

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.380
Don't move!

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:04.270
Help me!

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:06.520
I can't breathe!

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:19.830
It seems to have settled down.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:22.940
Bell, um... thank you.

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:24.140
Are you okay?

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:28.040
So this was an earthquake.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:31.340
Luna, have you experienced an earthquake before?

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:33.480
There were a few on the planet I lived on before.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:34.870
Yeah.

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:36.330
Get off already!

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:38.620
So I suppose earthquakes happen on this continent.

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:45.070
Seems okay over here too.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:47.240
Yeah, here's okay too.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:49.680
Should we check 'em all, just in case?

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:51.110
I guess so.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:23.390
There don't seem to be any edible things.

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:25.390
Howard!

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:30.140
Let's take a little break!

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:34.420
We haven't walked very far at all!

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:38.360
There's not going to be any food in the middle of all these rocks.

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:41.920
You were the one who said you were tired of just fish, weren't you Howard?

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:43.570
Maybe so...

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:44.810
Then stand up.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:47.170
I'm sure we'll find something.

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:50.240
Wait a moment!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:56.210
She really is stronger.

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:19.080
Can we eat this?

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:22.940
If we take out the thorns and cook it, it should be okay.

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:28.460
I vaguely remember my Mom doing it a long time ago.

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:29.580
Luna...

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:37.790
Alright! I'll get it!

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:39.480
Wait!

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:42.370
Let me see.

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:44.730
There don't seem to be any needles left behind...

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:48.480
I'm fine!

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:49.570
Really?

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:51.070
Look! See?

00:10:57.520 --> 00:10:59.390
Wait!

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:16.870
Help me!

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:21.780
What?

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.240
Ouch!

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:30.710
Damn him!

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:31.940
You're still going to try?

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:40.230
Hey!

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:42.930
Everyone!

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:45.710
Come look for a second!

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:56.730
How's that?

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:57.780
Chicks!

00:11:58.010 --> 00:11:59.170
They're so cute!

00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:01.310
So there was a nest in a place like this.

00:12:01.310 --> 00:12:02.840
I want those.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.280
I was chasing after it, thinking it could be food.

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.010
You got chased after!

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:19.530
And then I found this nest and thought it was so cute, I had to show all of you.

00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:21.560
That's definitely the mom.

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:23.320
Then that one is the father?

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:26.810
Probably.

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:32.770
Crap! Run!

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:41.660
Adam!

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:43.490
Kaoru!

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:52.570
Does it hurt?

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:55.830
Ah, sure looks like it hurts.

00:12:57.070 --> 00:12:58.870
Make sure to disinfect it.

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:01.570
Once we get back, we'll do it right away.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:02.620
Okay!

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:05.020
But it's too bad about before.

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:07.490
Its intensity was amazing!

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:10.420
It was giving everything to defend its family.

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:11.660
That's true.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:13.870
Family...

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:47.510
And after all that, fish again.

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:49.510
You're full of complaints.

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:50.690
Well, c'mon!

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:53.360
Luna said she'd make a salad.

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:54.890
Luna did?

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:57.860
Can Luna make something like that?

00:13:58.190 --> 00:13:59.540
Well she said it.

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:01.910
A salad...

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.620
If it's true, it'll be the first in a while!

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:07.380
Where'd Luna go?

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:10.270
She went to the river to pull out the thorns.

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:12.670
What thorns?

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:15.410
Seemed like there was a plant with lots of thorns.

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:18.330
Bell, the fish will be cooked soon.

00:14:19.270 --> 00:14:22.010
I'm just going to check on her. Go on and eat.

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:24.820
Can we really eat that?

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:27.780
Luna said it would definitely be delicious.

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:30.410
I'm looking forward to it!

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:48.260
So, is it going well?

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:50.620
I'll be done soon, so just wait.

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:54.820
Can I help with anything?

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:56.540
No, I'm fine.

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:01.490
Hey, can I ask you something?

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:06.740
What kind of cooking did your mom do, Bell?

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:14.020
Because my mom died when I was little, she never taught me how to cook.

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:24.740
So even if I want to make everyone delicious food, I really have no confidence.

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:30.330
Anyways, I'll just do my best to make something good.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:33.930
Luna!

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:37.080
I wonder if the salad's done yet.

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:44.620
I'll be... family... Luna's... um...

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:50.810
I'll be your family, Luna!

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:57.110
What do you mean by that?

00:15:57.370 --> 00:15:59.110
So, um...

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:03.710
er, so... basically...

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:05.510
...how do I put it...

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:08.020
Weird Bell.

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:18.440
What kind of strange thing is Bell saying?

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:26.510
Howard, how was the salad?

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:34.530
What is it? Doing that suddenly creeps me out.

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:40.190
But Bell...

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:41.090
What?

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:42.560
Did something happen to Bell?

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:45.630
"I'll be your family, Luna!"

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:47.470
...he said!

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:55.940
What did he say? One more time!

00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:59.430
I'll be your family, Luna!

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:02.060
Bell said that to Luna?

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:04.530
Yeah. What's he saying?

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:08.770
That's, in a manner of speakin'...

00:17:08.990 --> 00:17:10.230
...a proposal!

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:12.230
A proposal?

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:14.020
D-don't tell me...

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:17.660
I mean, what other sense 'a bein' someone's family is there?

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:18.780
Really?

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:19.830
Gotta think so.

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:23.880
Bell and Luna... What did Luna answer?

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:25.760
Nothing much...

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:28.570
Hey, what's a proposal?

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:30.410
It means, "Let's get married!"

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:33.330
Bell said, "Let's get married," to Luna.

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:35.660
Isn't that great?

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:36.820
That's all?

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:38.320
I don't really understand.

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:39.410
Really.

00:17:39.520 --> 00:17:40.720
How shameless!

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:46.230
In a situation where we don't know if we'll live or die...

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:49.040
...is no time so be saying something like that!

00:17:49.570 --> 00:17:51.860
What are you angry about, Menori?

00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:53.170
I'm not angry!

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:56.880
Speaking of which, Menori, do you have someone you like?

00:17:57.670 --> 00:17:58.530
Someone I like?

00:17:58.530 --> 00:17:59.470
You have one?

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:00.590
She has one.

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:01.720
Who is it?

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:02.920
Don't tell me...

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:04.790
...it's me?

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:08.210
D-don't look at me with those scary eyes!

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:13.460
I wonder how that girl is doing back in the colony.

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:14.390
That girl?

00:18:14.390 --> 00:18:16.160
Shingo, even you?

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.820
I didn't expect it because I thought you were a child!

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:21.180
You can't tell a book by its cover, I guess.

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:23.920
We went skating together all the time.

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:27.370
I bet everyone's really good at it by now.

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:28.160
Everyone?

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:30.140
Yep! My little sister's friend.

00:18:30.740 --> 00:18:32.840
"Big Bro Shingo, take us there!" they said.

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:35.210
I took them so many times, so they asked me so often.

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:36.370
What's up with that?

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:37.940
That's just babysittin'.

00:18:38.020 --> 00:18:39.970
Don't say misleading things!

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:42.480
What? What's wrong?

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:43.380
Everyone!

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:45.260
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:18:46.340 --> 00:18:47.580
They're here, they're here!

00:18:47.840 --> 00:18:49.340
Hey, you two.

00:18:50.240 --> 00:18:51.030
What?

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:52.870
I heard.

00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:55.340
"I'll be your family, Luna!"

00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:59.660
A proposal out of the blue. I was surprised!

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:01.080
Proposal?

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:02.690
Stop it, Howard!

00:19:02.690 --> 00:19:03.520
Hey, hey!

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:07.310
Pretty bold of Bell to say it out of the blue, too.

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:10.570
Bell!

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:15.370
Well, I wonder if Luna likes Bell too!

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:18.710
Howard...

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.190
I like him.

00:19:33.220 --> 00:19:35.060
Hold on to Bell's share.

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:42.630
Everyone...

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:08.130
They're cute.

00:20:09.670 --> 00:20:12.260
A mother, a father, and children.

00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:14.960
They look like a happy family.

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:17.060
Luna, I...

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:18.780
Don't say anything.

00:20:18.970 --> 00:20:19.910
But...

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:21.290
I was happy.

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:23.280
You see, I...

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:26.810
...thought I had always been alone.

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:30.330
Chako was with me, of course...

00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:33.630
...but when I heard everyone talking about their families...

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:36.260
...of course I got lonely.

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:41.620
But someday I'll be able to make my own family.

00:20:41.990 --> 00:20:43.790
I realized that today.

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:47.920
I just think that's something way off in the future.

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:50.170
Sorry, Bell.

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:51.410
No.

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:52.720
It's okay.

00:20:53.170 --> 00:20:57.330
And right now I have a very important family: Everyone.

00:20:57.330 --> 00:20:58.640
So I'm not lonely.

00:20:59.090 --> 00:21:01.340
That's right. We're all a family.

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:11.130
Did everyone hear?

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:13.380
That's a nice story.

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:16.830
Being in love with someone seems like a good feeling.

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:17.920
It's true.

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:19.310
Right, Menori?

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:25.080
More importantly, stop eavesdropping, all of you!

00:21:27.030 --> 00:21:28.980
When did everyone get here?

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:32.280
Hey, don't mind the small things.

00:21:32.280 --> 00:21:35.510
Bell, let's get back quickly and eat that salad.

00:21:35.510 --> 00:21:37.190
You just want to eat it.

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:38.620
Now you!

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:40.310
Luna...

00:21:41.470 --> 00:21:42.440
I'm tired.

00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:43.680
Are you okay?

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:46.460
It's gotten dark, too. Let's go back.

00:21:48.140 --> 00:21:49.570
I'll carry you.

00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:51.520
Please.

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:57.180
His face is hot.

00:21:58.720 --> 00:22:00.330
Adam, are you okay?

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:02.960
A fever?

00:22:04.680 --> 00:22:06.670
But he was just fine a moment ago.

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:08.240
Why all of a sudden?

00:22:09.070 --> 00:22:10.870
Anyways, let's hurry back to the ship.

00:22:11.210 --> 00:22:11.920
Yeah.

00:22:12.110 --> 00:22:13.210
Get back and get him to bed.

00:22:30.440 --> 00:22:31.940
He's hotter than before.

00:22:32.210 --> 00:22:33.820
Impossible!

00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:43.270
What's wrong, Adam?

00:22:46.080 --> 00:22:47.960
Adam! Adam!

00:22:50.580 --> 00:22:51.440
Adam!

00:23:03.110 --> 00:23:07.310
The cause for Adam's fever is somethin's wrong with his nano-machines.

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.340
To get treatment for him, we arrive at the nearest terraformin' machine, but...

00:23:13.530 --> 00:23:18.590
Some spherical robots of unknown origin stop us from entering and attack us!

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:20.660
At this rate, Adam will...

00:23:21.290 --> 00:23:23.620
Please! Open the door!

00:23:25.420 --> 00:23:28.010
Next time: That's why I have to go!
